# Qwen3-Coder-Next — 80B/3B MoE, coding specialist.
#
# Repo id verified against the HF API 2026-09-07: public, apache-2.0, not gated.
# The previous value here, "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next-80B-A3B-Instruct", does not exist (401);
# the real name carries no size/variant suffix.
HF_REPO="Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next"
HF_REVISION="a7fbcb5c0e12d62a448eaa0e260346bf5dcc0feb"

# BLOCKED: this is NOT a 1x H100 model, and the README's "cheap anchor" line is wrong.
#
#   79.7B params x 2 bytes (BF16)  = ~159 GB of weights
#   one H100 (PCIe or SXM5)        =   80 GB
#
# A3B means 3B *active* parameters per token; all 80B must still be resident. The FP8
# sibling (Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next-FP8, ~80 GB) does not rescue it either: that is the whole
# card before a single KV-cache block, and MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144 is a large allocation.
#
# So this needs at least 2x H100 with the FP8 checkpoint, or 4x for BF16. Two open
# questions before this can be set, neither of them a config detail:
#
#   1. FP8 vs BF16. Every other model in the lineup is described as NATIVELY FP8 or MXFP4.
#      A post-hoc FP8 quantisation of a BF16 release is a different object, and running the
#      anchor quantised while the others run native means the harness is no longer the only
#      thing held constant. That is a study-design call (AI-3158).
#   2. Capacity. Lambda has 1x, 2x and 8x H100 types; there is no 4x, and 8x had zero
#      capacity in every region when this was checked. BF16 may simply not be schedulable.
#
# TP/INSTANCE_TYPE are deliberately left at values that CANNOT silently launch something
# too small: fix them together with the decision above.
TP=2
MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144
# vLLM refuses tool_choice:"auto" without BOTH of these, and the harness agent loop
# sends exactly that on every call — so an attempt cannot even start without them
# (AI-3159). The parser is per-model-family, which is why it lives here rather than
# in the held constants.
# Parser choice: Chat template emits <tool_call>/<tool_response>/<tools>; qwen3_coder is the
#   Qwen-Coder parser and matches both family and format.
EXTRA_ARGS="--enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder"
INSTANCE_TYPE="gpu_2x_h100_sxm5"   # $8.38/hr live, NOT the $2.49 the plan assumed
